# Webhook Form Submission Automation

## Project Name

Webhook Form Submission Automation using n8n

---

## Objective

The objective of this project is to build an event-driven workflow using the n8n Webhook node. The workflow receives form data through a webhook, validates the submitted information, stores it in Google Sheets, and sends a confirmation email to the user.

---

## Workflow

Webhook → Edit Fields → IF (Validate Data) → Google Sheets → Gmail

---

## Features

- Receive form data using a Webhook
- Validate submitted information
- Save submitted data to Google Sheets
- Send a confirmation email to the user
- Test the workflow using Postman

---

## Technologies Used

- n8n
- Postman
- Google Sheets
- Gmail
- Webhook

---

## Workflow Description

1. The Webhook node receives a POST request from Postman.
2. The Edit Fields node organizes the submitted data.
3. The IF node validates the submitted information.
4. Valid data is appended as a new row in Google Sheets.
5. A confirmation email is sent to the submitted email address.

